       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-31 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>BJP and Opposition Clash Over Mock Parliament and Electoral Allegations</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A political debate emerged after the opposition INDIA bloc held a mock parliament at Mallikarjun Kharge's residence, passing an impeachment motion against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. BJP National Spokesperson Sanju Verma criticized the move, stating that a street veto can never replace democratic ethos and dismissing the proceedings as theatrics. Meanwhile, Congress MP Dr. Abhishek Manu Singhvi defended the event, highlighting widespread public concern and alleging that the Election Commission's affidavit conceals more than it reveals.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-31/bjp-and-opposition-clash-over-mock-parliament-and-electoral-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the public proceeding led by Rahul Gandhi, opposition leaders accused the election chief of treason, electoral manipulation, and unauthorized alterations of Form 6. Verma countered that the ruling government consistently agreed to discussions while Rahul Gandhi remained absent from the House. Furthermore, Prime Minister Narendra Modi declared at the Statue of Unity that India has successfully eliminated Naxalism and Maoist terror.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate, concise, and captures all key attribution and subject details from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/video/mock-parliament-row-street-veto-can-never-replace-democratic-ethos-says-bjps-sanju-verma-ytvd-3029548-2026-10-31?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
