     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-31 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Canada-Based Man Detained for Illegal Drone Flight in Kochi</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Police in Mattancherry detained 66-year-old Ashu Kumar Khanna for flying a drone without authorization near a highly sensitive area. The site includes the historic Kadavumbhagam Synagogue, Coast Guard premises, and the Indian Navy's INS Dronacharya training establishment. Khanna, a Punjab native settled in Canada, was booked under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita and Drone Rules before being released with a notice.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-31/canada-based-man-detained-for-illegal-drone-flight-in-kochi.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This security breach follows a recent alleged arson attack on the 800-year-old synagogue. Authorities previously invoked the Unlawful Activities (Prevention) Act against a suspect in that earlier case, highlighting heightened security concerns in the region.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately details the detainee's background, the sensitive nature of the location, and the legal charges.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/punjab-native-detained-for-flying-drone-illegally-in-high-sensitive-area-near-synagogue-in-keralam/article71648361.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/kochi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kochi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
