     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-10-31 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>France Braces for Third Weekend of Protests as Youth Rallies Spread Across Europe</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#World News</span> <span>#Protests</span> <span>#France</span> <span>#Europe</span></div>
       <p>France is preparing for a third consecutive weekend of protests on Saturday, October 31, 2026, driven by concerns over living costs and education. These demonstrations are part of a broader wave of youth-led rallies sweeping across Europe. Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez issued a warning of a “very high risk” of disorder, particularly “especially after dark on Halloween.” Authorities have deployed 70,000 police and gendarmes, matching the number mobilised a week prior, and rerouted the Paris march to the capital's outer boulevards, from Porte de Bagnolet to Porte de Charenton. Union and “yellow vest” marches through the city centre were banned, a restriction upheld by courts after challenges.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-31/france-braces-for-third-weekend-of-protests-as-youth-rallies.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>President Emmanuel Macron had stated on Monday, October 26, 2026, that marches would be kept out of city centres to protect shops. Police also imposed entry bans to Place de la Republique and Les Halles, areas affected by rioting and looting on October 17, from 11 p.m. to 6 a.m. on both Saturday and Sunday. A separate 9 p.m. curfew for unaccompanied minors was set around the Champs-Elysees, although a Paris court on Wednesday, October 28, 2026, had suspended an earlier curfew on minors, deeming it an illegal infringement of freedom of movement. The movement originated with high school students protesting deteriorating school conditions and expanded to encompass broader anger over the cost-of-living crisis and sluggish growth.</p><p>Nationwide, approximately 550,000 protesters were counted on October 17, an event that saw rioters loot hundreds of shops. Last Saturday (October 24, 2026), rallies involved 410,000 participants and were largely peaceful, though police made over 1,300 arrests. Paris police reported confiscating various forbidden items but described the situation as calm during last week's demonstrations. The ongoing unrest is putting mounting pressure on President Macron’s centrist administration amid the nationwide movement.</p><p>The youth-led protests are not confined to France. In Germany, a youth initiative named “Gen Z regelt” (roughly “Gen Z's got this”) called for demonstrations in some 30 cities, advocating for “education, health, climate protection and an affordable life,” and against any return of military conscription, with over 140,000 people signing up online. Berlin police anticipated around 10,000 attendees at the Brandenburg Gate, while some shops on Kurfuerstendamm boulevard preemptively boarded their windows. In Barcelona, Spain, Catalan police activated their highest-level alert following calls for new gatherings by an anonymous TikTok network, Blocus, after rioting there last Saturday led to about 130 arrests, mostly minors. Italian police are also on alert after clashes in Milan, Turin, and Bologna, with protest calls circulating on TikTok in Belgium, the Netherlands, Austria, Switzerland, and Portugal.</p><p>What to watch: The intensity and spread of youth-led protests across Europe, particularly on Halloween night.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Thorough and accurate synthesis of the full text covering numbers, locations, and political context well.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/france-heads-into-third-weekend-of-protests-as-youth-led-rallies-sweep-europe/article71649225.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
