     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-31 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India Celebrates Rashtriya Ekta Diwas Marking Sardar Patel's Birth Anniversary</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>India observed Rashtriya Ekta Diwas, celebrating the 151st birth anniversary of Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel. Prime Minister Narendra Modi led 'Ekta Parv' celebrations at the Statue of Unity in Gujarat, where he reviewed a National Unity Parade and inaugurated 31 development projects worth 426 crore rupees. The event featured a flag guard contingent led by women personnel.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-31/india-celebrates-rashtriya-ekta-diwas-marking-sardar-patels-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the ceremony, Modi administered a national unity pledge focused on preserving India's integrity and security. Political discourse surrounding the day included debates between the BJP and Congress regarding Patel's historical legacy and current national security challenges, while opposition parties concurrently held a mock parliament session.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively synthesizes the multifaceted report, covering both the official Ekta Diwas celebrations and the political events mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/video/rashtriya-ekta-diwas-pledge-dedicated-to-sardar-patel-for-national-unity-and-security-ytvd-3029434-2026-10-31?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
