       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-31 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>J&amp;K L-G Sinha Orders Intensified Crackdown on Terror Modules</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Jammu and Kashmir Lieutenant Governor Manoj Sinha has directed security and administrative officials to intensify actions against terror modules, counter-infiltration grids, and radicalization. During a high-level security review, he mandated monthly reviews of property attachments linked to narco-terrorists and those supporting terrorism to dismantle the terror ecosystem.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-31/jk-l-g-sinha-orders-intensified-crackdown-on-terror-modules.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Sinha emphasized that communal harmony and law and order must be preserved, calling for improved coordination between the J&amp;K Police, Army, and civil administration. He further ordered the establishment of district-level social media cells to counter misinformation and directed officials to ensure the availability of essential winter commodities.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the security meeting directives, the focus on communal harmony, and the administrative measures mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/l-g-sinha-orders-sustained-crackdown-on-terror-modules-in-kashmir-seeks-monthly-review-of-properties-ws-blrt-10406793.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
