     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-31 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Karnataka Cabinet Approves Uppara Community Hall Site in Kalaburagi</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Karnataka Cabinet has approved the allotment of a civic amenity site in Kusanur village, Kalaburagi, for the construction of a community hall for the Uppara community. Minister Priyank Kharge confirmed the decision, noting that the 439.67-square-meter site, located in Survey No. 19/2B, will be managed by the district Uppara Sangha.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-31/karnataka-cabinet-approves-uppara-community-hall-site-in-kal.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This approval addresses a long-standing demand from the community, which officials described as socially and economically disadvantaged. The proposed facility is intended to host cultural programmes and community activities, providing a dedicated space to support the welfare and development of the Uppara population within the region.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the cabinet decision, including the specific location and size of the site.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/cabinet-approves-site-for-uppara-community-hall-in-kalaburagi/article71645743.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
