     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-31 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Rayudu Questions Kuldeep Yadav's Exclusion After India Concedes Record T20I Total</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#India Cricket</span> <span>#T20I</span></div>
       <p>Former India batter Ambati Rayudu has sharply criticized the team's selection strategy during the fourth T20 International against New Zealand, held at Auckland on October 30, 2026. His comments followed a match where New Zealand posted an imposing 259 for 7 across their 20 overs, marking India's highest-ever total conceded in T20 cricket. Rayudu specifically questioned the decision to exclude left-arm wrist-spinner Kuldeep Yadav from the playing XI.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-31/rayudu-questions-kuldeep-yadavs-exclusion-after-india-conced.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Rayudu, speaking on Cricbuzz, elaborated on the tactical oversight, linking it to the venue's dimensions. &quot;Axar Patel and Naman Dhir bowl fast. But when you want batters to hit to the square boundaries because of the short straight boundary, you have to slow it up. That is where India could have used Kuldeep in this game to slow things up and force the batters to hit to the longer square boundaries,&quot; he stated, suggesting Kuldeep could have mitigated the scoring onslaught.</p><p>Kuldeep Yadav had not featured in any match during the New Zealand series prior to this fourth T20I, despite having played in two matches during India's preceding home series against West Indies. His potential value in the Auckland game was underscored by his strong record against in-form New Zealand batter Glenn Phillips, whom he had dismissed four times across five innings.</p><p>Rayudu further highlighted the mismatch between the Indian bowlers' natural style and the ground's characteristics. He noted, &quot;The Indian bowlers rely on fuller deliveries. So when your strength is bowling full, and the boundary size is small, you know if you miss, it's going to go big. The strengths of Arshdeep, Prince and Nitish are bowling full. And on this ground, that has been reflected in the final score.&quot;</p><p>What to watch: How India's team management addresses bowling strategies and spinner selections in subsequent T20 fixtures.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Thoroughly captures Ambati Rayudu's tactical analysis on Kuldeep Yadav's exclusion during the India-New Zealand match.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/india-could-have-used-kuldeep-yadav-ambati-rayudu-criticises-team-selection-during-new-zealand-t20is/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
