     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-31 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>RBI Digital Fraud Rules: 85% Compensation from 2027</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Personal Finance</span> <span>#Digital Fraud</span> <span>#RBI</span></div>
       <p>Starting January 1, 2027, victims of digital banking fraud in India may be eligible to receive compensation covering 85% of their net financial loss. This new provision, as per Livemint Money, aims to provide a clearer recovery mechanism for those affected by online scams.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-31/rbi-digital-fraud-rules-85-compensation-from-2027.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>For ordinary savers and taxpayers, this means a significant portion of funds lost to digital fraud could be recovered, provided they meet eligibility criteria. The report highlights the importance of understanding the complaint filing deadline and the maximum amount recoverable through this route. Adhering to these procedural details will be crucial for claiming compensation.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on eligibility criteria, the exact complaint filing deadlines, and the specified maximum compensation limits.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately covers the Livemint Money report on digital banking fraud compensation rules starting in 2027.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/rbi-digital-fraud-new-rules-jan-1-2027-how-much-compensation-can-you-claim-check-complaint-filing-deadline-11793443343615.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
