     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-31 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>South Africa Sets Australia 288-Run Target in Decisive Third Test</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>South Africa declared their second innings at 387, setting Australia a 288-run target to win the third Test at Newlands. Ryan Rickelton scored an unbeaten 101, his third Test century, alongside a 115-run contribution from Wiaan Mulder, leaving the series tied at 1-1 heading into the final day.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-31/south-africa-sets-australia-288-run-target-in-decisive-third.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Rickelton noted that the slow, deteriorating pitch at Newlands will challenge Australia’s pursuit, as maintaining a consistent run rate on the surface will be difficult. If successful, Australia would record the second-highest chase at the venue. Both sides face a decisive conclusion, with Rickelton highlighting that all three match results remain possible.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively synthesizes the source material, capturing the essential figures and the context of the match accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/ryan-rickelton-says-all-three-results-possible-ahead-of-final-day-in-cape-town/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
