       <h1>Stalin Demands Action Over MIDS Professor's Arrest</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>DMK president M.K. Stalin has called for action against police officials who arrested Madras Institute of Development Studies professor Kalaiarasan over a social media comment. Stalin argued that creating a society where there is no room for questions is detrimental to good governance, asserting that an administration should respond to criticism with ideas rather than police action.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-31/stalin-demands-action-over-mids-professors-arrest.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Stalin further demanded accountability for the virtual miscreants whose actions triggered the arrest. Additionally, the DMK leader condemned a separate incident involving the escape of an accused autorickshaw driver from the Kolathur police station, highlighting ongoing concerns regarding law enforcement conduct and administrative responsibility.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the political statement. The brief is concise and covers the core demands and criticisms made.</p>
